{
  "schemaVersion": 3,
  "id": "run",
  "name": "Run",
  "tagline": "Lattice · quicker and brighter: a stepping figure in phase with itself.",
  "description": "The Lattice at a quicker tempo, in a bright major colour: a stepwise figure in two lines that slide out of phase and lock, over a major chord and a drone, with harmonics above. The most energy in Field, and still no drums.",
  "use": {
    "name": "Routine",
    "for": "Getting through routine tasks quickly: admin, email triage, tidying, checklists.",
    "why": "Tempo is the one lever that reliably moves arousal (rule 29), and arousal tracks tempo rather than style or preference. Run raises tempo and brightness for shallow, quick work. Fast and loud together disrupted reading (rule 42, one study), so Run is kept away from reading, and its level is matched to everything else. Evidence: moderate for tempo and arousal; 138 bpm gained nothing over silence on speeded tasks, so there is no claim that it speeds you up."
  },
